    {
      "text": "Markets often miss second order implications until it shows up in direct statements. \n\n- If $LITE is completely sold out... (largely due to $NVDA bottlenecking everyone else, eg. securing Greensboro capacity), where else do your other companies like $AMD / hyperscalers / etc. get their supply procurement? \n\n- $SIVE is coming online with like 1/6th of the world's current laser capacity by themselves. (100M+ cw dfb lasers vs. 608M EML/CW globally per Trendforce). \n\nNot even including their partner foundries that they're targeting 2:1 for. \n\n- $AAOI is coming online with a ton of capacity too nex",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2108416144428421459",
      "time": "2026-10-09 12:35",
      "cashtags": [
